// Filename:	VSC90 Controller PCB.test
// Project:		VSC90
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    16-07-24
//
// Description: using the relay + nano for the power button.
//using the tenma PSU for the power to the PICKit4 
//Tests the 12V, 3.3V, I2C, EEPROM, USB, FTDI, motor and hall sensors
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.

#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box above.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
//DISPLAY: lamptrayPCB1.jpg
//CLICK_OK:

#2: Equipment Setup 1
a. Using TE159 connect the PSU to the Test box (TE209).
b. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the Test box (TE209).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable PSU.
d. Connect the PC to the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
//DISPLAY: TE132.jpg
//CLICK_OK:


#3: Equipment Setup 2
a. Connect the UUT to the Test box (TE209).
b. Connect the COAX PCB to the J3 on the UUT.
c. Place the UUT inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
d. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
//CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: I2C
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 0 // TURN RELAY OFF
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:5.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.300
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:0

#4.1: Power on the test box.
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 1 //TURN RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 0 // TURN RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF: //true result, current is good
GOTO: #4.2: 

IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the power button has been pressed, power supply, USB connection and the ftdi chip.		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1:


#4.2: Connect to the test box
a. If error message below is diplayed, click OK to continue. 
.
ERROR on line 71, CONNECT_ VSC90 - Not available 

DELAY: 9000 // GIVE TIME FOR THE pc AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90 // test connection to the FDTI chip
IF_NOT: // wrong FTDI porgram
GOTO: #4.3: // reprogram the FTDI and PIC
GOTO: #4.6: // FTDI is correct now check the PIC is programmed correctly 


#4.3: program the FTDI 
EXE: ftdi_programmer_vsc90.exe

#4.3.1: program the PIC
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:1
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000
GOTO: #4.4: // 

#4.3.2: program the PIC attempt 2 
DISCONNECT: VSC90
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:1
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000


#4.4:  Press the I/O Power button and turn on the test box
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 1 //TURN RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 0 // TURN RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 				
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4.4: // user didnt press the IO in time or there is fault 

#4.5: Connect again
DELAY: 7000 // GIVE TIME FOR THE pc AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4: // GO BACK TO THE START

#4.6: PCB Program version check.
COMMAND: VSC90  TYPE // Connection to the PIC chip
READLINE: VSC90  TYPE
Returned product is = %TYPE%
[%TYPE% STR_EQ VSC90] // evaluates inside the [] and set true or false flag
IF:
GOTO: #5: // checks and programming complete goto the start of tests
ELSE: // PIC is not programmed correctly still
IMPORTANT: Cannot program the test box (PIC). Please check connections to the PIC Kit and PCB.
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #4.3.2: // try programming the PIC again


#5: Voltage check
COMMAND: VSC90 ReadVolts
READLINE: VSC90 ReadVolts
Returned Voltage is = %ReadVolts%
RANGE: %ReadVolts% 12000 15					
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#7: Tests the I2C to the EEPROM and 3.3V supply
COMMAND: VSC90 ENUM
READLINE: VSC90 ENUM
Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = ZOOM,EEPROM,
Returned result is = %ENUM%
//CLICK_OK:
[%ENUM% STR_EQ ZOOM,EEPROM,] // evaluates inside the [] and set true or false flag
SUB: TestPassOrFail // sends the outcome to flag to the subroutine for evaluation


#8: USB3 and USB2 ports test
a. Test K6 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB3 enumerated is displayed.
b. Test K3 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB3 enumerated is displayed.
c. Test both ports on CONN7 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB2 enumerated is displayed. 
d. Test both ports on CONN6 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB2 enumerated is displayed. 
PASS_FAIL: #8


#9: Test filter wheel driver and hall sensor feedback.
a. Connect the Motor Driver and Hall Sensor Jig (TE212) to the CONN2 and J3 on the UUT.
b. Click OK to continue.
IMPORTANT: Ensure that the Brown cable is fitted in the correct orientation.
DISPLAY: Filterwheel.png
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: VSC90 C1h // home it
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: VSC90 C1X // read the vaule to check if the hall sensor is activated 
READLINE: VSC90 FILTER_Hall 
Returned result is = %FILTER_Hall%
RANGE: %FILTER_Hall% 1 0 // test if the hall sensor is activated
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#9.1: Test filter wheel driver and hall sensor feedback.
COMMAND: VSC90 CQ -450 // move it back to the hall sensor
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: VSC90 C1X // read the vaule to check if the hall sensor is activated 
READLINE: VSC90 FILTER_Hall 
Returned result is = %FILTER_Hall%
RANGE: %FILTER_Hall% 0 0 // test if the hall sensor is activated
SUB: TestPassOrFail



#10: Test Close up lens river and hall sensor feedback.
a. Connect the Motor Driver and Hall Sensor Jig (TE212) to the CONN5 and J1 on the UUT.
b. Click OK to continue.
IMPORTANT: Ensure that the Brown cable is fitted in the correct orientation.
DISPLAY: CloseUp.png
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: VSC90 C3=1				//1 = Move into optical path 
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: VSC90 C3X				// read the vaule to check if the hall sensor is activated 
READLINE: VSC90 CLOSEUP_Hall
Returned result is = %CLOSEUP_Hall%
// CLICK_OK:
RANGE: %CLOSEUP_Hall% 1 0
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#10.1:Test Close up lens river and hall sensor feedback.
COMMAND: VSC90 C3h// home it
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: VSC90 C3X
READLINE: VSC90 CLOSEUP_Hall
Returned result is = %CLOSEUP_Hall%
// CLICK_OK:
RANGE: %CLOSEUP_Hall% 0 0
SUB: TestPassOrFail



#11: Test complete
COMMAND: VSC90 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:


#Failed: A test failed
a. This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
b. Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: next test
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish.
DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:

COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
DISCONNECT: TENMAPSU
DISCONNECT: IC2
COMMAND: VSC90 C1Z
COMMAND: VSC90 C3Z
DISCONNECT: VSC90
// End of file
